# E23 -- Does an agitated surface wave respect the player's roster, or arrive from any species DF likes? This is v6.1's other safety question, and it is only now askable. The report listed E23 as blocked because `force` has no siege event on 53.16-r1.1 — but the trigger was never the timed event. DFHack's own shipped agitation-rebalance reads and writes the counters DF actually rolls on: plotinfo.outdoor_irritation against plotinfo.main.custom_difficulty.wild_irritate_min and wild_sens, with the chance for the next wildlife group being min(100, (irritation - min) * 100 / sens) and a hard gate at biome savagery > 65. So both arms run on MAGMA (savage 71) with wild_irritate_min 0, wild_sens 1 and outdoor_irritation pinned at 100,000 — every surface wave agitated by construction, re-pinned each sample so decay cannot lower it. One arm runs the tool with the land roster closed to its three largest entries; the control runs the same agitation with the tool off. A season, two replicates each. The fort may die; on a savage map with maxed agitation that is the result, not a failure.
run 20260918-200458 fort MAGMA backup MAGMA.preverify
